{
  "name": "cannavec-science",
  "version": "0.8.0",
  "description": "A grounding-and-verification layer that makes AI trustworthy for cannabis-science research. Five commands (research / ask / discover / verify / rigor): the model reasons over LIVE primary-source retrieval (PubMed, ClinicalTrials.gov, ChEMBL, and more), while deterministic code verifies every identifier is real and not retracted (PMID / DOI / NCT / ChEMBL / UniProt), enforces retractions, assigns GRADE, and runs safety + banned-pattern + phytochemistry-rigor detectors. Twenty-one curated science registries (≥ 230 rows) are kept as clearly-labelled offline reference the model reasons over — never the answer itself. The model proposes; deterministic code disposes. Stdlib-only Python ≥ 3.9; the verification core runs fully offline with 2,495+ unit tests. Mission: ground AI in credible, verifiable cannabis science so experts can trust it, use it, and love it.",
  "author": {
    "name": "Jack-MillionMedia",
